{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>I will sweep away</b> — Now he explained the phrase <i>man and beast, bird of the sky and fish of the sea</i>." "<b>And the meaning of \"the face of the ground\"</b> — the land of Israel." "<b>And the stumbling-blocks</b> — to the wicked alone the stumbling-blocks shall be; therefore <i>I will cut off man</i>, for they are wicked. And likewise he says to the humble: <i>perhaps you will be hidden</i>."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:12.612268634Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}